@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] mila-journey-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the device-key file hex codec: the `hex`/`unhex`
round-trip over arbitrary bytes, and `unhex` refusing odd-length and
non-ASCII text, accepting every even-length hex string and decoding to half
the input length. They MUST also cover the terminal-open readiness
classification, which retries only the exact closed readiness refusal codes.
The FFI-driven steps, trust fetch and approval flow are covered by the
mila-journey machine tests, not by properties.
